{"name":"Breezy Day","hex":"#bdc4b8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breezy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With a breeze blowing, with a lively wind, pleasantly windy.","With a cheerful, casual, lively and light-hearted manner."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breezy"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breezy","blocks":[{"text":"Breezy is a 1973 American romantic drama film directed by Clint Eastwood, produced by Robert Daley, and written by Jo Heims. The film stars William Holden and Kay Lenz, with Roger C. Carmel, Marj Dusay, and Joan Hotchkis in supporting roles. It is the third film directed by Eastwood and the first without him starring in it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Breezyfilmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breezy","wikidata":"Q653251"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c